				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">Druid Guide to rapid leveling for Lvl 24+</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=2772">cth24</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">10/26/2001 - 12:50 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2172">Steyr Atmee</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2173">Krispi</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														This is a little guide to how I've leveled over time and some good places to get experience that are often overlooked and underused. Here is the list by level:<br />
<br />
  24-31: Fear kiting!!! You were born to do it as a druid. Head to Everfrost and bind yourself at Halas. Watch those barbs, they don't shower much!! Now head to the tundra and track woolly mammoths. When you find one snare it and cast Terrorize Animal on it. As it runs beat the heck out of it from behind. It takes a while to kill them, but it's very mana efficient, so it keeps down time to a minimum. Be ready to fear again quick when your your spell breaks, as it's random in duration. Collect the nice tusks that drop and sell them for a cool 8-9pp each in Halas.  You'll find your bankroll rapidly swelling at this point.<br />
<br />
  31-35: Now that you're rich from the mammoths, gear up and head to Butcherblock again. Near Kaladim you'll find some crazed goblins on track that strangely con yellow or red. Get comfortable and pull these guys as quick as the pop. There are 3 that spawn. They drop 3-5pp, fs daggers, and ringmail pieces. GREAT exp, decent loot, and great faction in Kaladim. This camp can get crowded sometimes, so patience is a must here.  It's well worth it.<br />
<br />
  36-40: Now that you can med without staring at the darn book, it's time to try something a little tougher. Head to West Karana and go to the guard tower right next to the barbarian fishing village. Two guards, Konlan and McCluskey, spawn there. They are corrupt, so you can kill them and make positive faction in Qeynos. Nice, huh. Konlan is easy, but be careful with McCluskey. He resists fire well, so you may have to med kite him if your wis is not very high. When you kill these guys keep their guard bracelets. Take them to Capt Linarus in NK at the SK bridge guard tower.  Give them to him for wonderful exp and nice loot. The corrupt guards are rarely camped, so you should have this one to yourself most of the time.  This place rocks, so don't miss it!!!<br />
<br />
  41-44: Quad kite!!! This is an ability unique to us druids, so use it to your full benefit.  Head to Iceclad, making sure to have SoW and Gate memmed. The ring here is highly dangerous, so be prepared to run as soon as you arrive. Out of the portal take a right and head to the water. Follow the water till you come to a big island very close to the shore. This is where you'll pull to and med safely between kites. When at full mana head out and start snaring blue dire wolves. Keep Gate memmed in case you can't manage a pull. You're fighting right by the IC ring, so it's better to port out and come back. When you have 4 ensnared run around them till they are tightly grouped. Now blast away with Lightning Strike till they all die. This is not as easy as it sounds and takes practice. Don't be afraid to Gate if you screw up or get a bunch of adds. Smile now killer druid, as you'll get about 2 blues per quad kite. The exp will now fly by!!! <br />
<br />
  45-higher: Well, now you're where I am at this point. For great loot and so-so exp I've been quading ulthorks on the north coast of the Eastern Wastes. They drop plat, velium weapons, and ulthork armor.  Some of you have the ulthork armor that I've looted, so you know it's nice stuff.  You can also do frost giants for good exp and loot. <br />
<br />
Well druids, that's it. A quick and dirty little level guide that has worked wonders for me. As a druid you are unique in Norrath. No other class can match a druid's diverse group of skills and abilities. Use them all and have fun.  Give me holler if you have questions.<br />
<br />
Steyr Atmee<br />
Druid of the 45th Season						</td>
